@startuml deployment
!pragma layout smetana
' Status: Draft - Reconciliation Incomplete. AI-reconciled; not human reviewed (Principle VII).
' Written sources: docs/architecture/architecture.md section 2 (Runtime and deployment),
' and DEC-03 in specs/001-splitsmart-expense-sharing/decisions/decision-log.md.
' Layer dependencies are not drawn here. See component.puml.
title SplitSmart MVP Deployment (conditional draft: OC-1 open)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "User's computer\n(one computer, one signed-in user at a time)" as Computer {
  node "JVM process\n(the one running application process)" as Jvm {
    component "Swing UI layer" as Ui
    component "Service layer" as Service
    component "Domain layer" as Domain
    component "Repository layer" as Repository
    Ui -[hidden]down- Service
    Service -[hidden]down- Domain
    Domain -[hidden]down- Repository
  }

  rectangle "Exclusive single-instance lock\n(held through the one exclusive\ndatabase connection)" as Lock

  folder "Data folder: ${user.home}/.splitsmart\n(overridable with splitsmart.data.dir)" as DataFolder {
    database "SQLite database file" as Db {
      artifact "Receipt storage\n(receipts are held inside this file)" as Receipts
    }
  }

  node "Second launch of the application" as SecondLaunch
}

Jvm --> Lock : holds
Lock --> Db : protects
SecondLaunch ..> Lock : cannot get the lock;\nshows a message and exits

note top of Computer
  **OC-1 (web vs. desktop) is still open.**
  The customer asked for a primarily web-based product (CR-10).
  This desktop deployment does not satisfy that request.
  A web deployment would require redesign.
end note

note bottom of Computer
  **Limits (DEC-03):**
  People take turns on this computer and see each other's activity at next login.
  Roommates on separate computers cannot share data.
  Setting splitsmart.data.dir lets several OS accounts on this computer share a folder they can all write.
  Network shares and cloud-synced folders are **unsupported**.
end note

@enduml
